# Semgrep ignore file — suppress noise from generated/Electron/admin code.
# Each section has a rationale so future reviewers know why it's excluded.

# ── Built / minified assets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are the compiled output of the dashboard-ui Vite build. Findings here
# are duplicates of findings in the source files (already reviewed) and the
# minified form makes them unreadable anyway.
app/static/dashboard-react/

# ── Electron main-process files ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# lib/python-manager.js and lib/utils.js run inside the Electron main process,
# NOT in a browser renderer and NOT reachable from the network. child_process
# calls here are intentional — they launch the bundled Python backend and
# manage the local Python env. There is no user-controlled input path.
lib/python-manager.js
lib/utils.js

# proctor.py is the Electron renderer that connects to the FastAPI backend over
# localhost. Plain (non-TLS) WebSocket is correct here — the connection never
# leaves the machine. TLS-wrapped sockets would require a local certificate.
proctor.py

# config.js — the RegExp built from `name` is derived from a static list of
# known Electron API names, not from user input. ReDoS risk is negligible.
config.js

# ── HTML files with <link rel="canonical"> ───────────────────────────────────
# Semgrep's missing-integrity rule incorrectly fires on <link rel="canonical">
# tags. Canonical links are SEO hints — they don't load external resources and
# never execute in the browser. SRI is only relevant for <script> and <link
# rel="stylesheet"> tags that fetch and run external content.
app/static/download.html
app/static/register.html
website/index.html

# ── Admin / ops scripts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are developer-only migration and verification scripts that are never
# exposed to end users. The asyncpg f-string in verify_postgres_cutover.py
# uses a hardcoded table name list, not user input.
scripts/
